=== ISSUE ===
Title: README recommends putting the Lichess token in the chat (set_token) and in plaintext config

- The README's Configuration section offers `set_token` as an equal option. A token passed that way is stored in chat history and sent to the model provider.
- The Claude Desktop examples put the token in plaintext in claude_desktop_config.json.
- It says to put `.env` "in the project root", but dotenv reads `.env` from the server's working directory, which MCP clients usually set elsewhere.

=== PR ===
Title: docs: recommend passing the Lichess token from the OS secret store
Body:
Closes #<issue>

- New "Lichess Token" section ranks the options, most secure first: OS secret store at launch (macOS Keychain, libsecret, a password manager CLI), the client's env block, a .env file, and last `set_token`.
- Advises least-privilege token scopes, since some tools act on the account and the model reads other users' text.
- Claude Desktop examples now read the token from the Keychain.
- Removes the set_token example from "Account Management". The tool itself is unchanged.

